---
import Slide from '@decks/templates/Slide.astro';

// Named threads rather than sentences, so the slide reads as a list of
// things that are open rather than as four opinions.
//
// Target size came off. 24 is the 2.5.8 minimum and it clears AA on a
// fine pointer, and the touch case was answered in its own round, so
// raising it here would invite a challenge that has already been
// handled and take a slot from something genuinely unresolved.
//
// Character-level merging takes the slot (Matt, 2026-09-14). It follows
// straight on from the Multiplayer section the room has just watched, it
// is the only thread with a named external dependency, and saying what
// something costs and who you would need is a better last note than
// another thing that is merely unfinished.
//
// Say "a CRDT" out loud rather than only reading the line: the engineer
// on the panel will recognise it, and the two designers get the meaning
// from the title.
//
// Candidates that lost the slot, kept so they are not re-argued:
//   Read-only rows on a fine pointer. Carried as open in the record, but
//     smaller, and the touch half already answered itself.
//   Item variants, a tick versus an approval gate. The unbuilt boundary
//     round, and the best choice if this should end on a systems
//     question rather than an engineering one.
//   The one-level ceiling. The symptom is fixed; whether a parent should
//     be able to carry its subtree into another parent is still open.
//   Target size. Cut: 24 clears AA on a fine pointer and touch was
//     answered in its own round.
//
// Order is deliberate. The correctness problem first, because it is the
// one that would keep me up. Then the two questions I would want the
// room to answer. Then the one I would most like to be told I am wrong
// about.

const items = [
	{
		title: 'Autosave Failures',
		body: 'No Save button means no place for a failed write to land, which makes it silent data loss. The only correctness problem still open, and the first thing I would build.',
	},
	{
		title: 'More Nesting Levels',
		body: 'One level is a ceiling I chose, not one anybody asked for. Runbooks is the consumer most likely to want depth, and I would rather ask than find out.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Multiplayer Lock',
		body: 'Merging removes the reason for one. If people keep talking over each other in the same row, the answer is probably presence that is louder, not a lock.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Character-level Merging',
		body: 'Merging happens at save, not per keystroke, so two people typing for a minute diverge for a minute and then meet. A CRDT is the destination, and it is backend work: the text is one string today, and the activity stream, emails and search all expect it to stay one.',
	},
];
---

<Slide subtitle="Next Steps">
	<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-16 gap-y-10">
		{
			items.map((i) => (
				<div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
					<span class="text-strong text-3xl font-medium">{i.title}</span>
					<span class="text-subdued text-2xl">{i.body}</span>
				</div>
			))
		}
	</div>
</Slide>
